name brown-tagged
match c[a-z][0-9][0-9]
format brown_tagged
content word tag
# Words share canonical content. A tag is said of the word it tags, where it collides with every other tagging of that word;
# the sentence is its words, and the tags laid along it are no claim of its own: nothing else says that sentence, so
# nothing could collide with it.
thing token word
thing sentence of token
thing paragraph of sentence
relation "part of speech annotation" tag
attest token tag
